  "problem": "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=1+x+z-y,\\, & y(0)=1 \\\\ {z}^{′}=2-x+y-w,\\, & z(0)=1 \\\\ {w}^{′}=\\frac{3x+y}{2zw},\\, & w(0)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse Euler's Method with one step to approximate $y(1),$ $z(1),$ and $w(1).$\n\n$\\,y(1)≈$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,z(1)≈$\n{{field-2}},\n$\\,w(1)≈$\n{{field-3}}",
